1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,417
Tides is the macro layer: the big money flows behind every chart.

2
00:00:04,467 --> 00:00:08,757
Rates, the dollar, inflation, fear, credit, and where money is rotating.

3
00:00:08,807 --> 00:00:12,797
They move slowly, but they set the conditions every asset trades in.

4
00:00:13,265 --> 00:00:15,485
The Tide sums up twelve currents.

5
00:00:15,535 --> 00:00:20,742
Coming in means risk-supportive. Slack means mixed. Going out means risk-defensive.

6
00:00:20,792 --> 00:00:24,142
A new Tide only counts after five daily closes.

7
00:00:24,575 --> 00:00:29,056
The Sea state is how rough the water is: calm, moderate, rough, or storm.

8
00:00:29,106 --> 00:00:33,161
That's low to extreme volatility, from the VIX and Bitcoin.

9
00:00:33,609 --> 00:00:36,277
The winds apply the currents to each market.

10
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:40,595
A tailwind helps longs in that market. A headwind works against them.

11
00:00:41,058 --> 00:00:45,795
The calendar flags the big scheduled releases: the Fed, inflation, and jobs.

12
00:00:45,845 --> 00:00:49,772
A storm warning means an event is near. It isn't a forecast.

13
00:00:50,207 --> 00:00:54,411
The waves draw each current over time, with the swell they make together.

14
00:00:54,461 --> 00:00:57,918
Dashed lines mark past Fed, inflation and jobs days.

15
00:00:58,369 --> 00:01:03,384
Each current is scored against its own last five years, from very low to very high.

16
00:01:03,434 --> 00:01:08,384
Its pull says whether it's rising, falling, or flat, and which way that pushes risk.

17
00:01:08,823 --> 00:01:13,731
Beside the daily note, the AI Navigator answers questions about these readings.

18
00:01:13,781 --> 00:01:18,241
Today's AI Passage Plan applies them to your own assets and funnels.

19
00:01:18,672 --> 00:01:22,445
The plan covers the conditions, the week's events, the winds for your assets,

20
00:01:22,465 --> 00:01:24,391
the hazards, and things to watch.

21
00:01:24,441 --> 00:01:26,789
One plan a day, kept in your logbook.

22
00:01:27,222 --> 00:01:29,997
Macro conditions frame risk over weeks.

23
00:01:30,047 --> 00:01:34,805
They don't time trades, and a coin can rise on its own news while the tide goes out.
